<h4>The audience a preference is shown to is self-declared by the viewer (severity 2)</h4>
<p>Where: /Users/drashtipathak/Downloads/curbcut_check/force-app/main/default/classes/CurbCutShow.cls lines 57-65 and 92-94 (viewerRole is a string the caller chooses; the real user name is recorded beside it); docs/DECISIONS.md D13 acknowledges 'a viewer can name an audience they are not'. Criterion: Fairness (honour-system access to a disclosure).</p>
<p>Barrier or risk: A manager can read a statement the person restricted to 'My team' by choosing that role in the dropdown. It is recorded, so the person can find out afterwards, but a disclosure already made cannot be unmade. The acknowledgement in D13 is honest; the control is still after the fact.</p>
<p>Fix proposed: Derive the audience from the viewer's actual role (a permission set or a field on the user) rather than a dropdown, and keep the dropdown only for an explicit, logged 'read as a different audience' override that requires a written reason like the emergency path does.</p>
<p>Status: Open; second pass: upheld, Confirmed in source: CurbCutShow.forRecord (CurbCutShow.cls 57-65, 84, 92-94) only checks the caller's viewerRole string against three values and records UserInfo.getName() beside 'read as &lt;role&gt;'; curbCutHandoffBrief.js 34 and 74-120 feed it from a free 'I am reading this as' select defaulting to 'Manager only' on the Curb_Cut_Handoff_Record flexipage; no permission set, custom permission, user field or role is consulted anywhere in force-app; and the live /docs page (fetched, 301 KB) and docs/RAI-REFLECTION.md line 294 both list this exact finding as 'Status: Open' at severity 2. It cannot reach a real person yet, which is why severity should stay at 2 rather than rise: no production path sets Access_Preference__c.Access_Profile__c (CurbCutStanding.cls 119-124 sets only Statement, Scope, Shared_With and Auto_Apply; no class creates an Access_Profile__c; nothing passes accessProfileId to CurbCutIntake), so every preference saved through /ask, SMS, Slack, email or the agent is filtered out by CurbCutShow line 81 regardless of the dropdown, and only data/seed-scenarios.apex builds linked rows, where the one 'My team' preference (profiles[1], report 4) has no handoff attached, so the manager-reads-team scenario is not reproducible on the console today; with Private OWD and no sharing rules, the owner-level users who could ever use the brief can also read Statement__c straight from the Access_Preference tab layout with no ledger row, which is the larger version of the same gap.</p>
